Nf6 38. Kg3 Be1 39. Bc1 Bxf2 40. Rxf2 Qd3 41. Kh2 Nxe4 { With a close to winning position for Black. If } ) 
 ( 32. Bd7 $2 { then } Qe2 33. Rf3 Bxc3 $1 { is the easiest way to kill off this line. Next comes ...Nf6+ and a bishop check from the back. } ) 
gxf5+ 33. Qxf5 Qf4+ $1 { A clever idea, but White can refute it. } 34. Kxh5 $1 { After } ( 34. Qxf4 $2 Nxf4 35. Kxf4 Bxc3 36. Nf3 Ra1 37. Bb5 Rxa3 38. Bxc4 { White only makes a draw. } ) 
